# Chapters 7–8 sensor apps — the application Kconfig.
#
# This app defines no product knobs of its own (Chapter 8 adds
# the first); the file exists for the two lines at the bottom.
# Per-module log-level symbols for OUR driver do not appear by
# magic: they exist only where a Kconfig file instantiates
# Zephyr's log-config template for that module name (Chapter 2,
# Step 3 taught this; Chapter 4's driver app did it first). This
# does it for LD2410, creating CONFIG_LD2410_LOG_LEVEL_DBG and
# friends — which is what lets prj.conf aim the driver's log
# level without touching the application module.

module = LD2410
module-str = HLK-LD2410 driver (Chapters 4 + 7)
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
